        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[⚡ OpenBLD.net: Accelerating the DNS Path]]></title>
            <link>https://openbld.net/blog/accelerating-the-dns-path/</link>
            <guid>https://openbld.net/blog/accelerating-the-dns-path/</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[Reworking the core routing and filtering engine of OpenBLD for zero-allocation domain wildcard matching, multi-fold faster AWS Route 53 detection, and lower CPU overhead.]]></description>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="OpenBLD.net: Accelerating the DNS Path ⚡️" src="https://openbld.net/assets/images/openbld-fast-wildcard-dns-processing-update-a6bf72b2ebe5c9ed56e7746368be902b.webp" width="1250" height="680" class="img_tFOa"></p>
<p>Over the past few months, I have significantly reworked the core routing and filtering engine of <strong>OpenBLD.net</strong>. My primary focus is minimizing processing latency for every single DNS query.</p>
<!-- -->
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="whats-new">What's New<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/accelerating-the-dns-path/#whats-new" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What's New" title="Direct link to What's New" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<ul>
<li class="">⚡️ <strong>New domain wildcard matching engine</strong> - fast domain hierarchy matching without unnecessary memory allocations. A unified mechanism now powers three key components: <strong>Lua routing</strong>, <strong>allowlists</strong>, and <strong>blocklists</strong>.</li>
<li class="">⚡️ <strong>Multi-fold faster AWS Route 53 matching</strong> - a dedicated mechanism optimized for recognizing AWS DNS infrastructure domains several times faster.</li>
<li class="">⚡️ <strong>Reduced CPU utilization</strong> - resource-intensive regular expressions have been replaced with efficient algorithms wherever direct domain structure matching is sufficient.</li>
</ul>
<p>Less computation. Lower latency. Better performance.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="whats-next">What's Next<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/accelerating-the-dns-path/#whats-next" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What's Next" title="Direct link to What's Next" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>These optimizations lay the foundation for a <strong>major OpenBLD upgrade</strong> scheduled to roll out over the coming weeks.</p>
<p>Stay up to speed with <a href="https://openbld.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">OpenBLD.net</a>! 🚀</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <category>openbld</category>
            <category>dns</category>
            <category>performance</category>
            <category>golang</category>
            <category>engineering</category>
            <category>cybersecurity</category>
