        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[↗ How to Replace Local DNS in Ubuntu]]></title>
            <link>https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/</link>
            <guid>https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/</guid>
            <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[Step-by-step guide on disabling router DHCP DNS and configuring Cloudflare DNS (1.1.1.1) in modern Ubuntu/Debian distributions.]]></description>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="How to Replace Local DNS in Ubuntu" src="https://openbld.net/assets/images/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu-281ee484284b006f12fa0a1e232fb007.webp" width="1250" height="680" class="img_tFOa"></p>
<p>In modern Ubuntu distributions (20.04, 22.04, 24.04), domain name resolution is handled by <code>systemd-resolved</code>. A common issue occurs when you configure a public DNS (such as Cloudflare's <code>1.1.1.1</code>), yet the system continues to use the local router's DNS (<code>192.168.x.x</code>) obtained via DHCP.</p>
<!-- -->
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="what-is-the-issue">What is the issue?<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/#what-is-the-issue" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to What is the issue?" title="Direct link to What is the issue?" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>You can check your current DNS servers using the following command:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">resolvectl status</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>If the output looks similar to the example below, the specific network interface settings (<code>Link 2</code>) are overriding your global settings due to the <code>+DefaultRoute</code> flag:</p>
<div class="language-text codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-text codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">Global</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">         DNS Servers: 8.8.8.8</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain" style="display:inline-block"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">Link 2 (enp1s0)</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">         Protocols: +DefaultRoute -LLMNR -mDNS -DNSOverTLS</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">       DNS Servers: 192.168.1.1</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Simply editing <code>/etc/systemd/resolved.conf</code> only updates the <code>Global</code> section, which does not stop the DHCP client from assigning the router's IP address directly to the network interface.</p>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="solution-via-netplan">Solution via Netplan<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/#solution-via-netplan" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Solution via Netplan" title="Direct link to Solution via Netplan" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>To prevent the interface from accepting DNS settings from your router and enforce Cloudflare servers, you need to configure <strong>Netplan</strong>.</p>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="1-locate-the-configuration-file">1. Locate the configuration file<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/#1-locate-the-configuration-file" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to 1. Locate the configuration file" title="Direct link to 1. Locate the configuration file" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>Check the contents of the <code>/etc/netplan/</code> directory:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">ls -la /etc/netplan/</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Typically, you will find a file named <code>00-installer-config.yaml</code> or <code>50-cloud-init.yaml</code>.</p>
<div class="theme-admonition theme-admonition-caution admonition_mJjN alert alert--warning"><div class="admonitionHeading_On4P"><span class="admonitionIcon_KDIQ"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8.893 1.5c-.183-.31-.52-.5-.887-.5s-.703.19-.886.5L.138 13.499a.98.98 0 0 0 0 1.001c.193.31.53.501.886.501h13.964c.367 0 .704-.19.877-.5a1.03 1.03 0 0 0 .01-1.002L8.893 1.5zm.133 11.497H6.987v-2.003h2.039v2.003zm0-3.004H6.987V5.987h2.039v4.006z"></path></svg></span>Attention</div><div class="admonitionContent_oNyG"><p>If there are multiple <code>.yaml</code> files in the directory, edit the last one alphabetically, as it holds the highest priority and overrides the previous ones.</p></div></div>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="2-edit-the-configuration">2. Edit the configuration<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/#2-edit-the-configuration" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to 2. Edit the configuration" title="Direct link to 2. Edit the configuration" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>Open the file in a text editor (replace with your actual filename):</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">sudo nano /etc/netplan/00-installer-config.yaml</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Add the <code>use-dns: false</code> directive under <code>dhcp4-overrides</code> and specify Cloudflare's addresses in <code>nameservers</code> (make sure to use spaces for indentation, as tabs are invalid in YAML):</p>
<div class="language-yaml codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-yaml codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token key atrule">network</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">  </span><span class="token key atrule">version</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token number">2</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">  </span><span class="token key atrule">ethernets</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">    </span><span class="token key atrule">enp1s0</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token comment" style="color:rgb(98, 114, 164)"># Replace with your interface name from resolvectl status</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">      </span><span class="token key atrule">dhcp4</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token boolean important">true</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">      </span><span class="token key atrule">dhcp4-overrides</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">        </span><span class="token key atrule">use-dns</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token boolean important">false</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">      </span><span class="token key atrule">nameservers</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"></span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">        </span><span class="token key atrule">addresses</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">:</span><span class="token plain"> </span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">[</span><span class="token plain">1.1.1.1</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">,</span><span class="token plain"> 1.0.0.1</span><span class="token punctuation" style="color:rgb(248, 248, 242)">]</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="3-apply-the-changes">3. Apply the changes<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/#3-apply-the-changes" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to 3. Apply the changes" title="Direct link to 3. Apply the changes" translate="no">​</a></h3>
<p>Validate the syntax and apply the new configuration:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">sudo netplan apply</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="if-using-networkmanager">If Using NetworkManager<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/#if-using-networkmanager" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to If Using NetworkManager" title="Direct link to If Using NetworkManager" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>On Ubuntu Desktop or certain cloud images, Netplan might delegate network management to <code>NetworkManager</code> (<code>renderer: NetworkManager</code>). If the local DNS persists after running <code>netplan apply</code>, configure the interface directly via <code>nmcli</code>:</p>
<ol>
<li class="">
<p>Find the name of your active connection:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">nmcli con show</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
</li>
<li class="">
<p>Disable automatic DNS and set Cloudflare (replace <code>"Wired connection 1"</code> with your connection name):</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">sudo nmcli con mod "Wired connection 1" ipv4.ignore-auto-dns yes</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">sudo nmcli con mod "Wired connection 1" ipv4.dns "1.1.1.1 1.0.0.1"</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">sudo nmcli con up "Wired connection 1"</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
</li>
</ol>
<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="verify-the-result">Verify the Result<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-replace-dns-to-custom-ubuntu/#verify-the-result" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Verify the Result" title="Direct link to Verify the Result" translate="no">​</a></h2>
<p>Confirm that the local router's IP is gone and Cloudflare's servers are active on the interface:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">resolvectl status enp1s0</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Expected output:</p>
<div class="language-text codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-text codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">Link 2 (enp1s0)</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">    Current Scopes: DNS</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">         Protocols: +DefaultRoute -LLMNR -mDNS -DNSOverTLS DNSSEC=no/unsupported</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">Current DNS Server: 1.1.1.1</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">       DNS Servers: 1.1.1.1 1.0.0.1</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<div class="theme-admonition theme-admonition-tip admonition_mJjN alert alert--success"><div class="admonitionHeading_On4P"><span class="admonitionIcon_KDIQ"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 16"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M6.5 0C3.48 0 1 2.19 1 5c0 .92.55 2.25 1 3 1.34 2.25 1.78 2.78 2 4v1h5v-1c.22-1.22.66-1.75 2-4 .45-.75 1-2.08 1-3 0-2.81-2.48-5-5.5-5zm3.64 7.48c-.25.44-.47.8-.67 1.11-.86 1.41-1.25 2.06-1.45 3.23-.02.05-.02.11-.02.17H5c0-.06 0-.13-.02-.17-.2-1.17-.59-1.83-1.45-3.23-.2-.31-.42-.67-.67-1.11C2.44 6.78 2 5.65 2 5c0-2.2 2.02-4 4.5-4 1.22 0 2.36.42 3.22 1.19C10.55 2.94 11 3.94 11 5c0 .66-.44 1.78-.86 2.48zM4 14h5c-.23 1.14-1.3 2-2.5 2s-2.27-.86-2.5-2z"></path></svg></span>Tip</div><div class="admonitionContent_oNyG"><p>If you previously added other DNS servers to <code>/etc/systemd/resolved.conf</code> (e.g., <code>8.8.8.8</code>), comment them out and run <code>sudo systemctl restart systemd-resolved</code> to keep the <code>Global</code> section clean.</p></div></div>]]></content:encoded>
            <category>linux</category>
            <category>ubuntu</category>
            <category>networking</category>
            <category>dns</category>
            <category>netplan</category>
