        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[↗ Apply Git Path to Own Project]]></title>
            <link>https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-apply-git-path/</link>
            <guid>https://openbld.net/blog/how-to-apply-git-path/</guid>
            <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[A guide on how to apply a Git path in your projects.]]></description>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="How to Apply Git Path" src="https://openbld.net/assets/images/how-to-apply-git-patch-eb99fe0a3ed5a3493530c0302a087166.webp" width="1250" height="680" class="img_tFOa"></p>
<p>Patch files has <code>.patch</code> extension and are used to distribute changes to source code. They can be applied to a Git repository using the <code>git apply</code> command.</p>
<!-- -->
<p>As example I has <code>v0.2.4-http-sources.patch</code> file and want to apply it to my local repository.</p>
<p>Go to the repository directory and check the status of the repository:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">cd /path/to/benzine-gateway</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">git status --short</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>If the repository is clean, you can apply the patch, but first check what changes will be applied:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">git apply --check /path/to/v0.2.4-http-sources.patch</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>If the check is successful, you can apply the patch:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">git apply /path/to/v0.2.4-http-sources.patch</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>After applying the patch, you can check the status of the repository again to see the changes:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">git diff</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Add the changes to the staging area and commit them:</p>
<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_hvY0 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color:#F8F8F2;--prism-background-color:#282A36"><div class="codeBlockContent_g14S"><pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_EGYB thin-scrollbar" style="color:#F8F8F2;background-color:#282A36"><code class="codeBlockLines_WNl5"><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">git add config.go main.go gateway_test.go</span><br></div><div class="token-line" style="color:#F8F8F2"><span class="token plain">git commit -m "Allow HTTP and HTTPS list sources"</span><br></div></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Done!</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <category>openbld</category>
            <category>2026</category>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[🤝 OpenBLD and Unihost.kz 10y+ Stable Experience]]></title>
            <link>https://openbld.net/blog/openbld-and-unihost-kz-2026/</link>
            <guid>https://openbld.net/blog/openbld-and-unihost-kz-2026/</guid>
            <pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[OpenBLD and Sys-Adm.in have relied on infrastructure provided by Unihost.kz for over 10 years.]]></description>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="OpenBLD and Unihost.kz" src="https://openbld.net/assets/images/openbld-and-unihost-kz-2026-2ba9d4d40563d17a264f4bd7a8df2efb.webp" width="1250" height="680" class="img_tFOa"></p>
<p>For more than 10 years, OpenBLD and Sys-Adm.in have relied on infrastructure provided by Unihost.kz.</p>
<!-- -->
<p>This is the longest-running partnership in OpenBLD’s history. Reliable performance, high-quality network connectivity, and most importantly - the company’s generous, free-of-charge support helped make the launch of the public OpenBLD.net service possible.</p>
<p>Several servers in Almaty have remained part of our infrastructure throughout this period, including a dedicated uptime monitoring node, supporting both our services and the wider OpenBLD ecosystem.</p>
<p>More than a decade later, they are still doing their job.</p>
<p>Thank you, Unihost.kz, for supporting OpenBLD and helping us keep the Internet a little safer 🚀</p>
<h4 class="anchor anchorTargetStickyNavbar_m4Qy" id="updates">Updates<a href="https://openbld.net/blog/openbld-and-unihost-kz-2026/#updates" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Updates" title="Direct link to Updates" translate="no">​</a></h4>
<ul>
<li class="">Official <a href="https://t.me/openbld" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">Telegram</a></li>
</ul>]]></content:encoded>
            <category>openbld</category>
            <category>unihost.kz</category>
            <category>2026</category>
        </item>
